// UploadDataProductContentWithBodyWithResponse Upload a data product's content
//
// Writes the body to the path the product names, replacing whatever was there,
// and moves the product to `PROVISIONED`. A failed transfer leaves the status
// alone. Missing parent directories are created first.
//
// Requires a `WRITE` standing **on the product** — the same standing editing the
// record takes, since the path is part of the record. As with the download, no
// standing on the storage is needed.
//
// The content may be sent as the raw request body, which is what
// `curl --data-binary @file` sends, or as a `multipart/form-data` part named
// `file`, which is what a browser form sends. The remote name always comes from
// the product, never from a part's filename. Bodies are capped at 5 GiB.
//
